"""Assemble release evidence only; never read .env or secret.txt."""
import json, hashlib
from pathlib import Path
from datetime import datetime, timezone, timedelta
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
if (root/'scripts/phase4-postfix-release-baseline.json').exists():
    raise SystemExit('Historical pre-fix generator retired. Use node scripts/write-phase4-postfix-report.mjs after current final regressions.')
def read_json(name): return json.loads((root/name).read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig'))
reg=read_json('scripts/phase4-final-regression-results.json')
assert len(reg['results'])==10 and all(x['exitCode']==0 for x in reg['results']), 'Final regression run incomplete or failed'
db=read_json('scripts/phase4-database-inventory.json')
browser=read_json('scripts/phase4-browser-results.json')
p4=read_json('scripts/phase4-verification-results.json')
excel=read_json('scripts/phase4-spreadsheet-results.json')
report_counts=read_json('scripts/phase4-report-count-results.json')
assert report_counts['result']=='PASS'
audit=read_json('scripts/phase4-dependency-audit.json')
baseline=read_json('scripts/phase4-release-baseline.json')
changed=[name for name,h in baseline.items() if hashlib.sha256((root/name).read_bytes()).hexdigest()!=h]
assert not changed, 'Frozen release files changed'
stamp=datetime.now(timezone(timedelta(hours=8))).isoformat(timespec='seconds')
def table(head,rows):
    return '| '+' | '.join(head)+' |\n|'+ '|'.join(['---']*len(head))+'|\n'+ '\n'.join('| '+' | '.join(str(v).replace('|','\\|').replace('\n',' ') for v in row)+' |' for row in rows)+'\n'
out=[]
def section(title,text): out.append('## '+title+'\n\n'+text.strip()+'\n')
out.append(f'''# MedicAppointment — Final Verification and Release Readiness Report

**Timestamp:** {stamp}, Asia/Manila (UTC+08:00).

**Workspace:** D:\\Development\\Projects\\draft. **Release candidate:** current Phase 1–3 workspace, not merely Git HEAD; existing changes are uncommitted/untracked relative to the older repository baseline.

**Audit Scope**

Read the original audit and Phase 1, 2 and 3 reports first. On resume, PHASE4_CONTINUATION.md was absent; saved test outputs, the release checklist and 78-file SHA256 baseline supplied the recoverable state. The continuation file was then created. The final report was also absent. No existing Phase 1–3 changes were reverted. Completed checks were reused, followed by the explicitly requested complete final regression run.

No production deployment, hosted database reset, real patient query/deletion, hosted demonstration seeding or external SMS send occurred. Tests created disposable loopback PostgreSQL databases and synthetic records only. Actual browser requests to non-loopback endpoints were intercepted; remote WebSockets were replaced with an offline loopback endpoint. Existing .env values were not printed. secret.txt was privately classified without displaying values. A nondefault Git whitespace diagnostic emitted source context; subsequent checks captured and sanitized Git output rather than reproducing source lines. No application or database-source feature changes were made in Phase 4.

**Evidence classifications:** CONFIRMED means demonstrated at the stated local/mocked boundary; PARTIAL means implemented/tested with an explicit remaining limitation; NOT VERIFIED means the integration/environment was not exercised. Traceability uses FIXED, ACCEPTED LIMITATION, NOT VERIFIED and STILL BROKEN. None of these labels equates local SQL/mocked Auth with a configured hosted Supabase installation.

**Freeze evidence:** all {len(baseline)} files in scripts/phase4-release-baseline.json still match. Original audit and Phase 1–3 reports were preserved. The only pre-existing verification file corrected was scripts/test-phase2-ui.mjs: fixed sleeps became bounded request-condition waits, with all assertions retained. Added Phase 4 scripts/artifacts/checklist/continuation/report provide verification only.
''')
section('A. Executive Summary','''The release candidate passes clean installation of dependencies, TypeScript/Vite build, static verification, all Phase 1–3 regressions, offline Edge type checking, additional Phase 4 database checks, Chrome/Edge synthetic browser checks and normal Excel CSV opening. The critical role-escalation and unrestricted appointment-write defects are closed in the tested local schema. Privacy-safe availability, schedule validity, exact-slot concurrency and Manila time handling remain protected.

This is **not a production approval**. No real Supabase Auth/PostgREST/browser chain, hosted migration, live scheduler, live Realtime, provider delivery or production role audit has been verified. The final npm dependency audit still exits 1 with three moderate and one high vulnerable package classifications. A tracked file contains anon-role JWT material; no service-role JWT/password was identified by the categorical scan, but current validity, repository history and deployed default accounts remain unverified.

| Target | Classification | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| School demonstration | **NOT READY for a complete connected demonstration** | Local synthetic demonstrations and code/test walkthroughs work. A real isolated Auth/database rehearsal and configured demonstration environment are still missing; mocked HTTP must not be presented as hosted functionality. |
| Staging deployment | **READY WITH PREREQUISITES** | Reviewed incremental files are locally executable; staging ownership/extensions/Auth/schema cache/secrets, backups and synthetic E2E must be configured and tested. |
| Real production | **NOT READY** | All staging integration/operational evidence, security hygiene, dependency review, role review, recovery and notification procedures remain prerequisites. |

No new application release-blocking defect was confirmed during Phase 4. Initial additional-test failures were fixture/adapter/selector expectations; they were corrected without weakening application safeguards. Existing limitations and verification gaps are explicitly listed below.''')
section('B. Release Candidate Architecture','''React 18.3, React Router 6 declarative BrowserRouter/Routes, TypeScript and Vite form the SPA. Installed lockfile versions include Vite 5.4.21, esbuild 0.21.5, react-router/react-router-dom 6.30.6 and @supabase/supabase-js 2.116.0. package-lock.json version 3 agrees with package.json root dependencies and devDependencies.

src/App.tsx mounts independent patient and staff providers. src/lib/supabaseClient.ts creates clients with persistent/auto-refreshing sessions, URL detection disabled, storage keys medical-patient and medical-appointments-staff. usePortalAuth/portalIdentity/asyncState resolve one identity packet atomically, reject wrong roles, clear stale patient/profile state, apply initialization/query deadlines and unsubscribe. signOut uses local scope.

Ten public application tables, RLS, column ACLs, SECURITY DEFINER functions with explicit safe search_path and EXECUTE ACLs implement the backend. Appointment browser writes are SELECT-only plus approved ownership/admin RPCs. All patient/staff availability and writes share _clinic_schedule_slots/_assert_slot_bookable. PostgreSQL timestamptz stores instants; clinicTime.ts supplies Manila dates/times/ranges/weeks.

Appointment mutation invalidation refreshes local mounted views. The staff auth provider owns one debounced appointment Realtime subscription; patients have no global feed. Optional publication installation is separate.

Phase 3 SQL creates an appointment-versioned SMS outbox/ledger. send-confirmation verifies Auth and SQL ownership; send-reminders uses CRON_SECRET; notification-status verifies a Twilio signature. Worker claims/leases and result persistence distinguish provider acceptance from later delivery. Vault-backed five-minute scheduler installation is separate. Reports use admin-only complete SQL aggregation and paged audit RPCs, with shared spreadsheet-safe CSV encoding.

Required migrations, Edge folders/configuration, scheduler/publication files, environment example and verification scripts exist. .env.example has only fake placeholders for the three public frontend variables and server-only variable names in comments.''')
