section('R. Remaining Known Limitations','''**HIGH / release prerequisites:** actual staging Auth/PostgREST/JWT/RLS/RPC ownership/schema cache; real-data migration preflight/backups/restore rehearsal; historical admin legitimacy; private tracked-material/history and deployed demo-account review; dependency security resolution or formally bounded applicability acceptance; correct function secrets/origins/gateway; real notification provider/callback/scheduler verification if advertised operational.

**MEDIUM / operational limitations:** exact-start protection does not prevent old-grid duration overlaps; identity histories are not automatically merged; demographic duplicates require review; uncertain/stubbed/in-flight messages require reconciliation; five-message worker capacity unmeasured; real Realtime isolation/reconnect unknown; full staff browser mutations/live password changes and expired Auth sessions remain unverified; exported data needs authorized storage/import procedures.

**LOW / accepted:** old SQL header demonstration/setup hints are subordinate to the explicit current README/setup and deployment inventory (never use demo full.sql/seed.cjs for hosted upgrades); >500 kB bundle warning; blank invalid nested route/no application error boundary; long-open midnight rollover refresh; some bounded lookups/list snapshots/performance suggestions; note-reading/independent room-save absent; no invented email/PDF/Excel export/print/destructive archive features.

Dependency audit exact snapshot: four packages, three moderate/one high, zero critical. Vite 5.4.21/esbuild 0.21.5 include development-server disclosure/path issues. The high Windows filesystem-deny bypass requires exposed development-server conditions; static dist serving does not run that server. Keep development loopback-only and never deploy Vite dev/preview as a public clinical server. The maintainer lists patched Vite branches including 6.4.3; any toolchain upgrade must be deliberate and rerun all tests. [Vite upstream advisory](https://github.com/vitejs/vite/security/advisories/GHSA-fx2h-pf6j-xcff).

React Router 6.30.6 is flagged for untrusted navigation redirects and SSR constructor injection. Source uses hardcoded internal navigation/declarative BrowserRouter, with no SSR hydration. SSR advisory explicitly excludes Declarative Mode; redirect applicability is an inference from current fixed-target calls, not a vulnerability remediation. Reassess if untrusted navigation/SSR is added. The lockfile remains flagged; do not claim clean dependency security. [Redirect upstream advisory](https://github.com/remix-run/react-router/security/advisories/GHSA-wrjc-x8rr-h8h6), [SSR upstream advisory](https://github.com/remix-run/react-router/security/advisories/GHSA-337j-9hxr-rhxg).

Full sanitized package/advisory/fix metadata: scripts/phase4-dependency-audit.json. npm audit --json exited 1; its diagnostic wrapper succeeded in saving that result. No npm audit fix --force or major Router/toolchain migration was performed during feature freeze.''')
