section('T. School Demonstration Readiness','''**NOT READY for the requested complete connected demonstration.** Safe local SQL test demonstrations, code walkthroughs and actual-browser synthetic transport exercises are successful. They can demonstrate implementation evidence, but must be labelled as synthetic/mocked and cannot establish live registration, persisted clinic flows or automation.

Before raising to READY WITH KNOWN LIMITATIONS: configure a disposable local Supabase-compatible full stack or explicitly authorized isolated staging with synthetic Auth identities; install reviewed schema/migrations; bootstrap admin safely; rehearse complete patient and staff flows through actual Auth/PostgREST; verify direct refresh; establish provider-stub messaging and openly identify scheduler/Realtime limitations. Never use real patient data or seed a hosted database with the local seeder. A notification-disabled/manual-refresh demonstration may be acceptable only if those limitations are explicitly declared.''')
section('U. Staging Readiness','''**READY WITH PREREQUISITES.** The candidate builds, local fresh and compatible incremental SQL installations pass, and security/lifecycle regressions are preserved. No confirmed new application blocker prevents a deliberate isolated staging trial.

Prerequisites: authorized isolated project/local complete stack; compatible owner/extensions/Auth policies/RPC schema cache; backups and real preflight review if upgrading; appropriate exact origins/server secrets/Vault; synthetic accounts and destinations created through deliberate Auth/admin operations; dependency/hygiene review; full real HTTP RLS/role attack and UI rehearsal. Claiming reminders or Realtime additionally requires installed live job/publication and observed outcomes. This classification authorizes no automatic deployment.''')
section('V. Production Readiness','''**NOT READY.** Local tests cannot establish deployed RLS, Auth, privacy, backups, existing data validity, historical role legitimacy, live messaging/scheduler/Realtime, or patient-operational readiness. The flagged dependency tree and repository/demo hygiene need a documented disposition.

Production requires all staging gates, actual protected credential/account review, migration rollback/restore plans and ownership/ACL checks, synthetic adversarial REST and concurrency evidence, real-browser patient/staff flows, truthful notification consent/destination/quota/unknown-send operations, signed callback/cron verification where enabled, secure static hosting/HTTPS/history fallback, monitoring/support responsibility and approved historical schedule/link reconciliation rules. No real patient information was used to shortcut those checks.''')
